## CodeGraph usage

Use CodeGraph to understand dependency and collision. NOT to guess fields.

| Task | Use CodeGraph for |
|------|-------------------|
| Explore schema | canonicalFields, docxSlots, renderBindings |
| Explore apply runners | Clone safety pattern |
| Explore audit rules | Understand issue flags |
| Trace BM field path | Avoid duplicate/collision |
| Trace compiler | Ensure no manual compiled-v2 edit |

## Skill selection for corpus work

| Skill | When to use |
|-------|-------------|
| `review-bugbot` | Review plan/apply runner before write |
| `unittest-skill` | Write tests for guard/apply runner |
| `babysit` | Keep branch/commit clean, merge-ready |
| `output-skill` | Prevent report truncation |

## Apply workflow (single candidate)

```
1. review packet → proposed decision
2. human approve
3. apply 1 mutation
4. validate
5. compile
6. audit
7. publish
8. sync
```

## Safety gates (ABS brakes)

Check before any mutation:

1. No cross-BM evidence
2. No label-only if domain label ≠ domain path
3. No approved decision risk > MEDIUM without reviewer approval
4. No rawPattern EMPTY approved
5. No textBefore only `{{document.fieldN}}` approved
6. No compiled-v2 manual edit
7. No locked contract mutation outside approved decisions
8. COMPILED_DRIFT not increased
9. SOURCE_MISMATCH not increased
10. totalIssues not increased
